('127.461.d.2.A',4,'A message gets lost when a nurse uses medical words that the patient does not know. This is a barrier to:','["walking", "understanding", "hearing aids", "breathing"]'::jsonb,1,'Jargon blocks understanding.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.B',3,'A patient is anxious about surgery. The best communication response is to speak calmly and:','["leave the room", "change the subject", "listen to the concerns", "tell them to stop worrying"]'::jsonb,2,'Empathy helps anxious patients.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.B',4,'A patient who speaks little English needs care. A health worker should arrange for a qualified:','["driver", "cook", "decorator", "interpreter"]'::jsonb,3,'Interpreters bridge language gaps.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.C',3,'Two coworkers disagree about a schedule. A good conflict-resolution technique is to listen to both and look for a:','["compromise", "rumor", "winner", "punishment"]'::jsonb,0,'Compromise settles conflicts.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.C',4,'Techniques such as staying calm, using I statements, and focusing on the problem work best when the goal is to:','["win the argument", "solve the conflict", "embarrass a coworker", "avoid talking"]'::jsonb,1,'Resolution is the aim.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.D',3,'Knowing that the prefix hyper means above normal, a nurse understands that hypertension means blood pressure that is:','["too low", "normal", "too high", "absent"]'::jsonb,2,'Word parts reveal meaning.','original'),
('127.461.d.2.D',4,'In carditis, the root cardi names the organ that pumps blood and itis means inflammation, so carditis is inflammation of the:','["stomach", "lungs", "liver", "heart"]'::jsonb,3,'Medical terms combine word parts.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.A',3,'A person who motivates others, stays honest, and makes fair decisions shows the traits of a good:','["leader", "bystander", "rival", "critic"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders model good traits.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.A',4,'Responsibility, integrity, and the ability to inspire a team are examples of:','["hospital rooms", "leadership traits", "exam questions", "fixed salaries"]'::jsonb,1,'Traits make leaders effective.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.B',3,'A student officer in HOSA organizes a service project and thanks volunteers. This demonstrates:','["confusion", "avoidance", "leadership skills", "absence"]'::jsonb,2,'Leaders organize and recognize others.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.B',4,'A team leader who takes responsibility for a mistake and helps fix it shows:','["blame", "rumors", "delay", "accountability"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaders own their results.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.C',3,'At a meeting, the chair uses an agenda and gives everyone a chance to speak. This helps the group to:','["stay organized and fair", "create conflict", "run out of time", "avoid decisions"]'::jsonb,0,'Agendas focus meetings.','original'),
('127.461.d.3.C',4,'Taking minutes during a meeting creates a record of what was decided and who will:','["order supplies", "do each task", "win the debate", "pay for lunch"]'::jsonb,1,'Minutes record actions.','original'),
('127.461.d.4.A',3,'A student uses a state labor website to compare the pay and training needed for several health careers. This is researching:','["movie times", "sports scores", "career options", "recipes"]'::jsonb,2,'Reliable sources show career data.','original'),
('127.461.d.4.A',4,'To judge whether an employment website is reliable, a student should check who runs it and whether the data are:','["loud", "long", "colorful", "current and sourced"]'::jsonb,3,'Credible sources matter.','original'),
('127.461.d.4.B',3,'Choosing to leave school early can limit a person''s later job options. This shows a career decision can have long-term:','["effects", "sounds", "rains", "colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Choices have consequences.','original'),
('127.461.d.4.B',4,'A student weighs the cost of training against the pay of a career. This is thinking about the causes and effects of a:','["sports game", "career decision", "weather forecast", "school bus route"]'::jsonb,1,'Planning compares costs and benefits.','original'),
('127.461.d.6.A',3,'An X-ray technologist helps find disease, while a physical therapist helps people recover movement. These careers are in the diagnostic and:','["retail areas", "farming areas", "therapeutic areas", "culinary areas"]'::jsonb,2,'Careers are grouped by function.','original'),
('127.461.d.6.A',4,'A medical laboratory technician tests blood samples, while a nurse delivers daily care. The lab technician works in the diagnostic area, and the nurse works mostly in the:','["accounting office", "research office", "sales department", "therapeutic area"]'::jsonb,3,'Different pathways serve different roles.','original'),
('127.461.d.6.B',3,'A patient with a broken leg may see an emergency physician, a radiology technologist, and a physical therapist. These team members work together to deliver:','["complete care", "slow care", "unrelated care", "confusing care"]'::jsonb,0,'Care depends on teamwork.','original'),
('127.461.d.6.B',4,'The respiratory therapist tells the nurse that the patient needs more oxygen. This sharing of information between team members improves:','["billing only", "patient care", "scheduling only", "parking"]'::jsonb,1,'Collaboration improves outcomes.','original'),
('127.461.d.7.A',3,'A doctor, a nurse, a pharmacist, and a dietitian work together to plan a patient''s care. This is the concept of:','["isolating", "avoiding", "teaming", "competing"]'::jsonb,2,'Teams provide quality care.','original'),
('127.461.d.7.A',4,'When team members respect each other''s roles and share information, the patients receive:','["less care", "confusing care", "slower care", "safer, better care"]'::jsonb,3,'Teaming improves quality.','original'),
('127.461.d.7.B',3,'HOSA-Future Health Professionals and the American Nurses Association are examples of:','["professional organizations", "film studios", "sports teams", "grocery stores"]'::jsonb,0,'These groups support training and standards.','original'),
('127.461.d.7.B',4,'A professional organization helps its members by offering continuing education and setting standards for their:','["hobbies", "work", "vacations", "hairstyles"]'::jsonb,1,'Associations support the profession.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.A',3,'A code of ethics lists the duties of a profession, while a scope of practice describes what a worker is legally allowed to:','["wear", "own", "do", "eat"]'::jsonb,2,'Scope sets legal limits.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.A',4,'A certified nursing assistant is asked to give a medicine only a nurse may give. Staying within the scope of practice, she should:','["do it quietly", "guess the dose", "ask a patient", "decline and tell the nurse"]'::jsonb,3,'Workers follow their scope.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.B',3,'A health worker who tells a stranger about a patient''s illness has broken:','["confidentiality", "a schedule", "a dress code", "a vacation"]'::jsonb,0,'Privacy must be protected.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.B',4,'HIPAA is a law that protects the privacy of a patient''s:','["bus pass", "health information", "car insurance", "school grades"]'::jsonb,1,'HIPAA protects medical data.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.C',3,'Questions about who gets a limited organ for transplant, or whether to continue treatment, are called ethical issues in:','["fashion", "sports", "health care", "cooking"]'::jsonb,2,'Hard choices arise in medicine.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.C',4,'A patient with a serious illness decides to refuse treatment. Ethically, a competent patient has the right to:','["lose all privacy", "be ignored", "be forced to accept care", "make decisions about care"]'::jsonb,3,'Autonomy is a core principle.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.D',3,'When a health worker fails to give care that a reasonable worker would give and the patient is harmed, it may be called:','["negligence", "kindness", "fundraising", "teamwork"]'::jsonb,0,'Negligence is failure to meet the standard of care.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.D',4,'A legal responsibility for harm caused by a mistake in care is called:','["punctuality", "liability", "luck", "charity"]'::jsonb,1,'Liability carries legal risk.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.E',3,'Health workers must follow state and federal laws, such as those about reporting suspected abuse and protecting:','["lunch menus", "uniform colors", "patient records", "parking rules"]'::jsonb,2,'Laws guide practice.','original'),
('127.461.d.8.E',4,'Licensing laws exist to ensure that health workers have the proper training and are:','["wealthy", "well-paid", "famous", "qualified to practice"]'::jsonb,3,'Licensure protects the public.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.A',3,'A patient decides on her own which treatment to accept after hearing the options. This is an example of:','["autonomy", "neglect", "pressure", "isolation"]'::jsonb,0,'Autonomy means self-determination.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.A',4,'A patient chooses not to have a procedure after a clear explanation of the risks. The health worker should respect the patient''s:','["need for punishment", "right to decide", "ability to pay", "wishes only if the family agrees"]'::jsonb,1,'Respect autonomy.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.B',3,'Getting vaccines and washing hands are wellness strategies that help prevent:','["rain", "traffic", "disease", "homework"]'::jsonb,2,'Prevention reduces illness.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.B',4,'Regular screenings, such as a blood pressure check, are used to find problems early, which supports the prevention of:','["hydration", "good sleep", "exercise", "serious disease"]'::jsonb,3,'Early detection saves lives.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.C',3,'A supportive friend who encourages exercise has a positive effect on a person''s physical and mental health. A relationship that adds constant stress can have a:','["negative effect", "pleasant effect", "no effect ever", "positive effect"]'::jsonb,0,'Relationships affect health.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.C',4,'Being isolated for a long time can increase the risk of depression. This shows the effect of relationships on:','["finances only", "mental health", "weather", "road safety"]'::jsonb,1,'Social ties matter.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.D',3,'A patient''s bill of rights tells patients they have the right to respectful care and to know the:','["staff schedules", "hospital mascots", "risks of treatment", "cost of supplies"]'::jsonb,2,'Rights protect patients.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.D',4,'An advance directive documents what kind of care a person wants if she can no longer speak for herself. It records her:','["phone number", "bill", "school record", "choices"]'::jsonb,3,'Directives record wishes.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.E',3,'A hospital serves patients of many backgrounds, so staff learn about different customs, diets, and beliefs. This shows an understanding of:','["diversity", "uniformity", "isolation", "competition"]'::jsonb,0,'Diversity affects care.','original'),
('127.461.d.9.E',4,'A patient''s religion forbids certain foods. A good health worker will accommodate the diet whenever it is:','["unusual", "medically safe", "loud", "too inconvenient"]'::jsonb,1,'Respect cultural practice.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.A',3,'The World Health Organization and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention are examples of:','["restaurants", "sports leagues", "regulatory and health agencies", "game companies"]'::jsonb,2,'These agencies set health guidance.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.A',4,'OSHA is a government agency that sets rules to keep health workers safe on the:','["stage", "field trip only", "bus", "job"]'::jsonb,3,'OSHA protects workers.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.B',3,'Wearing gloves and washing hands between patients follow industry safety standards called:','["standard precautions", "parking rules", "dress codes", "hospital menus"]'::jsonb,0,'Standard precautions prevent infection.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.B',4,'A rule that every hospital must have clear exit routes and working extinguishers is a standard for fire:','["decorating", "safety", "billing", "parking"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety rules include fire safety.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.C',3,'Using a sharps container for used needles protects workers and patients from:','["boredom", "noise", "injury and infection", "hunger"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe disposal prevents harm.','original'),
('127.461.d.10.C',4,'A health worker who reports a spill in a hallway right away and puts up a warning sign prevents:','["hunger", "late bills", "long meetings", "falls"]'::jsonb,3,'Hazard reporting prevents accidents.','original'),
('127.461.d.11.A',3,'Hospitals use equipment such as ultrasound machines, heart monitors, and ventilators in diagnostic and:','["therapeutic care", "marketing", "sports", "cooking"]'::jsonb,0,'Technology aids diagnosis and treatment.','original'),
('127.461.d.11.A',4,'An electrocardiogram machine records the heart''s electrical activity, so it is used mainly to:','["clean floors", "diagnose heart problems", "wash laundry", "cook meals"]'::jsonb,1,'Different devices serve different tasks.','original'),
('127.461.d.11.B',3,'A monitor shows an error code and gives odd readings. A health worker should suspect a possible:','["lunch break", "new patient", "equipment malfunction", "staff meeting"]'::jsonb,2,'Odd readings may indicate a problem.','original'),
('127.461.d.11.B',4,'A smoking smell and sparks from a medical device are signs of a malfunction that can endanger patients and staff, so the device should be:','["ignored", "used faster", "covered up", "taken out of use"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety comes first.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
