from (values
('127.461.d.11.C',3,'If a device is not working correctly, a health worker should follow the facility''s process by reporting it to a:','["supervisor or biomedical staff", "competitor", "stranger", "patient''s visitor"]'::jsonb,0,'Reports go through proper channels.','original'),
('127.461.d.11.C',4,'Documenting what happened with a faulty device, with the date and equipment number, helps the facility to:','["hide the problem", "track and fix problems", "raise prices", "avoid training"]'::jsonb,1,'Reports support repair and safety.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.A',3,'A student who enjoys lab work and plant science visits a seed company to see what biotechnology workers do. This visit is a way to determine:','["a grade level", "a bus route", "interest in the field", "a tax rate"]'::jsonb,2,'Exploration reveals interests.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.A',4,'Job shadowing a lab technician helps a student learn whether the daily tasks match his:','["wardrobe", "phone plan", "lunch order", "interests and abilities"]'::jsonb,3,'Experience guides decisions.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.B',3,'Quality control analyst, research technician, and fermentation operator are all jobs found in:','["biotechnology", "farming only", "shipping only", "retail only"]'::jsonb,0,'Many careers exist in biotech.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.B',4,'A student who wants a career testing the purity of vaccines would look at jobs in:','["sports marketing", "quality control", "fashion design", "food service only"]'::jsonb,1,'Quality control tests products.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.C',3,'To find accurate information on pay and training for biotechnology careers, a student should check a government labor site or a:','["advertisement", "random video", "professional organization website", "gossip blog"]'::jsonb,2,'Reliable sources provide accurate data.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.C',4,'A career source is more reliable when it names the author, gives a date, and cites its:','["bank balance", "favorite color", "mascot", "sources of data"]'::jsonb,3,'Credible sources are documented.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.D',3,'A student writes a short summary of her skills, education plans, and career goals in biotechnology. This helps her:','["communicate her qualifications", "avoid school", "skip research", "hide her interests"]'::jsonb,0,'Self-description supports applications.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.D',4,'A student who tells an advisor that she excels at lab math and plans on a two-year degree is communicating her knowledge and:','["birthday", "educational level", "favorite song", "street address"]'::jsonb,1,'Advisors need these details.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.E',3,'A lab technician job is conventional, while a job that combines biology with art, such as science illustration, is a:','["required class", "mandatory test", "non-conventional opportunity", "school rule"]'::jsonb,2,'Unusual careers also use biotech knowledge.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.E',4,'A woman who is a scientist and wants to teach science to children may find opportunities in a:','["factory line only", "standard laboratory only", "retail store only", "non-conventional career"]'::jsonb,3,'Careers can be blended.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.F',3,'Using bacteria to make insulin is a biotechnology application in:','["medicine", "music", "fashion", "sports"]'::jsonb,0,'Biotech makes medical products.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.F',4,'Microbes that clean up an oil spill are an application of biotechnology to the:','["courtroom", "environment", "stage", "playground"]'::jsonb,1,'Bioremediation helps the environment.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.G',3,'A student searching a science database must evaluate whether a source is credible. A source is more reliable if it was:','["unsigned", "posted anonymously", "peer reviewed", "an advertisement"]'::jsonb,2,'Peer review checks quality.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.G',4,'When researching a topic online, a student should compare information from several sources to check for:','["speed", "colors", "fonts", "accuracy and bias"]'::jsonb,3,'Cross-checking reduces error.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.H',3,'A student reads an article in an academic journal. These articles report original research and are usually reviewed by other:','["scientists", "coaches", "actors", "chefs"]'::jsonb,0,'Peer review is by experts.','original'),
('127.462.d.1.H',4,'To read a scientific article critically, a student should look for the question, methods, results, and the:','["menu", "conclusion", "crossword", "advertisement"]'::jsonb,1,'Articles follow a structure.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.A',3,'Debates about genetically modified foods and the use of human genetic data raise current ethical and legal:','["costumes", "holidays", "issues", "menus"]'::jsonb,2,'Biotech raises hard questions.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.A',4,'Deciding who owns the rights to a gene sequence is a legal question, while deciding whether it is right to alter embryos is an:','["scheduling question", "weather question", "tax question", "ethical question"]'::jsonb,3,'Law and ethics both matter.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.B',3,'Early farmers practiced selective breeding long before DNA was understood. Biotechnology therefore has a long:','["history", "speed limit", "menu", "price"]'::jsonb,0,'Biotech began with breeding and fermentation.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.B',4,'The announcement of the cloned sheep Dolly raised public concern about the ethics of:','["tourism", "cloning", "furniture", "recycling"]'::jsonb,1,'Cloning triggered debate.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.C',3,'Two biotechnology topics, such as gene therapy and genetically modified crops, each involve legal and technology issues. A student who compares them is discussing the topics'' legal and:','["music concerns", "spelling concerns", "technology concerns", "color concerns"]'::jsonb,2,'Both law and technology shape biotech.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.C',4,'A patent gives an inventor exclusive rights to a new biotechnology process for a set time. A patent is a:','["recipe", "tax", "grade", "legal protection"]'::jsonb,3,'Patents protect inventions.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.D',3,'A claim about a new gene therapy is supported by lab data and measurements. Evidence that can be measured is called:','["objective evidence", "personal feeling", "opinion", "rumor"]'::jsonb,0,'Objective evidence is measurable.','original'),
('127.462.d.2.D',4,'A person''s feeling that a food is unsafe, without test data, is a view supported by:','["peer review", "subjective evidence", "objective evidence", "controlled trials"]'::jsonb,1,'Personal belief is subjective.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.A',3,'The Food and Drug Administration, the Environmental Protection Agency, and the Department of Agriculture are agencies that regulate:','["fashion", "sports", "biotechnology products", "video games"]'::jsonb,2,'Federal agencies oversee biotech.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.A',4,'A company that wants to sell a new drug made with biotechnology must have it approved by the:','["NFL", "IRS", "NASA", "FDA"]'::jsonb,3,'The FDA approves drugs.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.B',3,'The Biotechnology Innovation Organization represents companies in the industry and helps shape:','["policy and standards", "fashion trends", "bus schedules", "school lunch"]'::jsonb,0,'Groups influence rules.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.B',4,'Professional organizations help set guidelines that biotechnology labs follow to keep work:','["expensive", "safe and ethical", "slow", "secret"]'::jsonb,1,'Standards guide practice.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.C',3,'Rules that say work must be done in a documented, consistent way, such as good laboratory practices, are called:','["rumors", "suggestions", "regulations", "jokes"]'::jsonb,2,'Regulations set requirements.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.C',4,'GMP stands for good manufacturing practice, which means products are made and checked in a way that ensures their:','["speed", "cost", "color", "quality and safety"]'::jsonb,3,'GMP ensures consistent quality.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.D',3,'A lab keeps a written step-by-step procedure for each test so every technician follows the same method. These are called:','["standard operating procedures", "school rules", "menus", "weather reports"]'::jsonb,0,'SOPs keep results consistent.','original'),
('127.462.d.3.D',4,'A technician records the date, sample, and result of each test in a lab notebook so that the work can be:','["hidden", "reviewed and repeated", "forgotten", "sold"]'::jsonb,1,'Records support quality.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.A',3,'The journals Nature and Science are examples of professional:','["clubs", "games", "publications", "stores"]'::jsonb,2,'Journals share research.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.A',4,'A professional publication for biotechnology workers may include articles about new techniques, news about the industry, and:','["music lyrics", "clothing ads", "game scores", "job announcements"]'::jsonb,3,'Industry publications cover jobs and news.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.B',3,'Companies that make crops, those that make medicines, and those that make industrial enzymes are different biotechnology industry:','["sectors", "colors", "hobbies", "holidays"]'::jsonb,0,'Biotech has many sectors.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.B',4,'A company producing biofuels from algae belongs to the biotechnology sector of:','["fashion retail", "industrial or energy biotechnology", "sports media", "banking"]'::jsonb,1,'Biofuel is an industrial application.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.C',3,'A student studies the training, pay, and demand for a lab technician job and shares the findings in a short report. She is investigating and reporting on:','["shopping malls", "sports leagues", "career opportunities", "music genres"]'::jsonb,2,'Career research guides plans.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.C',4,'The Occupational Outlook Handbook lists job outlook, pay, and:','["vacation spots", "team colors", "favorite foods", "required education"]'::jsonb,3,'Handbooks list requirements.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.D',3,'Joining HOSA or a local biotechnology club lets a student meet professionals and practice skills through:','["a professional organization", "a shop", "a hotel", "a bank"]'::jsonb,0,'Clubs connect students to the field.','original'),
('127.462.d.4.D',4,'A state biotechnology association offers networking events that help members find:','["restaurants", "jobs and mentors", "fashion", "video games"]'::jsonb,1,'Networking opens doors.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.A',3,'A lab technician writes a clear email, speaks politely on the phone, and listens during a meeting. These are examples of:','["lab techniques", "driving skills", "communication skills", "cooking skills"]'::jsonb,2,'Communication takes many forms.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.A',4,'A worker uses email and a shared online document to send results to a team member in another city. This is:','["a letter by post", "a face-to-face talk", "a phone call by wire", "electronic communication"]'::jsonb,3,'Electronic tools connect teams.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.B',3,'For a lab job interview, a good applicant brings a resume, dresses neatly, and arrives:','["early", "next week", "late", "after lunch"]'::jsonb,0,'Interview skills help secure jobs.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.B',4,'Showing up on time, following directions, and learning new tasks help a worker to:','["lose a job", "keep a job", "skip training", "avoid feedback"]'::jsonb,1,'Good habits maintain employment.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.C',3,'Greeting coworkers politely and respecting their space and time are examples of workplace:','["rivalry", "jargon", "etiquette", "secrecy"]'::jsonb,2,'Etiquette shows respect.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.C',4,'Keeping a phone silent during a meeting and not interrupting others show good:','["pride", "laziness", "noise", "workplace manners"]'::jsonb,3,'Manners support a positive environment.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.D',3,'A technician who stays focused, finishes tasks on time, and asks for help when stuck shows productive:','["work habits", "rumors", "delays", "excuses"]'::jsonb,0,'Habits drive productivity.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.D',4,'A positive attitude at work includes accepting feedback and being willing to:','["blame others", "learn new things", "quit quickly", "avoid tasks"]'::jsonb,1,'Positive attitude supports growth.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.E',3,'Wearing goggles, gloves, and a lab coat while handling chemicals are examples of safety:','["souvenirs", "entertainment", "equipment", "decorations"]'::jsonb,2,'PPE protects workers.','original'),
('127.462.d.5.E',4,'Texas workers can learn about their right to a safe job from the:','["local theater", "sports network", "school cafeteria", "Texas Workforce Commission and OSHA"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety rules come from agencies.','original'),
('127.462.d.6.A',3,'Brewing beer uses yeast to ferment sugars. The yeast is a living organism that changes the sugars into alcohol and carbon dioxide. This is a biotechnology:','["manufacturing process", "sports event", "board game", "fashion show"]'::jsonb,0,'Fermentation is a classic process.','original'),
('127.462.d.6.A',4,'Producing insulin in engineered bacteria is a process whose end product is a:','["fabric", "medicine", "fuel", "toy"]'::jsonb,1,'Biotech produces drugs.','original'),
('127.462.d.6.B',3,'If a biotechnology plant dumps untreated waste into a stream, living things in the stream and nonliving factors such as water pH can be:','["improved", "entertained", "harmed", "unchanged always"]'::jsonb,2,'Waste impacts ecosystems.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
