from (values
('127.472.d.3.D',4,'A technician who repeats a patient''s question back to be sure she understood is showing a trait of:','["ineffective communication", "carelessness", "effective communication", "avoidance"]'::jsonb,2,'Clarifying helps accuracy.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.E',3,'A prescription says bid. Knowing that this abbreviation means twice daily, the technician correctly reads and communicates:','["jokes", "riddles", "slang", "medical vocabulary"]'::jsonb,3,'Abbreviations must be accurate.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.E',4,'Translating the abbreviation prn on a label into plain words for a patient, which means as needed, shows the ability to:','["communicate medical vocabulary", "sell medicine", "order supplies", "clean shelves"]'::jsonb,0,'Technicians must be clear.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.F',3,'A noisy pharmacy makes it hard for a patient to hear counseling. One way to remove this barrier is to move to a:','["louder spot", "quiet private area", "outer lobby", "busier counter"]'::jsonb,1,'Reduce noise and distraction.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.F',4,'A patient does not understand a drug label written in complex words. A helpful way to remove this barrier is to use:','["more jargon", "larger words", "plain language", "longer sentences"]'::jsonb,2,'Plain language aids understanding.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.G',3,'For a patient who is hard of hearing, a technician can face the patient, speak clearly, and provide information in:','["fast speech", "whispers", "a different room", "writing"]'::jsonb,3,'Adapt to the person.','original'),
('127.472.d.3.G',4,'A customer with limited English needs help. The technician should ask for a qualified:','["interpreter", "driver", "salesperson", "decorator"]'::jsonb,0,'Interpreters help communication.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.A',3,'Planning tasks, setting priorities, and handling interruptions are examples of time management, and breathing exercises and breaks are examples of:','["billing", "stress management", "pricing", "inventory control"]'::jsonb,1,'Both help performance.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.A',4,'When a pharmacy begins using new software, the technician learns the system and adjusts. This is called:','["time travel", "inventory", "change management", "delay"]'::jsonb,2,'Change requires adaptation.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.B',3,'Negotiation, empathy, and cooperation are examples of:','["math skills", "laboratory skills", "driving skills", "interpersonal skills"]'::jsonb,3,'People skills matter.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.B',4,'A technician who disagrees with a coworker over a work schedule uses negotiation by:','["finding a solution both can accept", "demanding to win", "refusing to talk", "complaining to patients"]'::jsonb,0,'Negotiation seeks agreement.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.C',3,'When a prescription label is missing information, the technician finds out what is needed and follows the right steps to fix it. This is:','["avoidance", "problem-solving", "delay", "denial"]'::jsonb,1,'Problem-solving needs a plan.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.C',4,'After a recurring error in label printing, the pharmacy changes its checking process. This shows implementing an effective:','["complaint", "delay", "solution", "mistake"]'::jsonb,2,'Solutions prevent repeats.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.D',3,'The Texas State Board of Pharmacy sets the minimum standards of practice that pharmacy workers must:','["avoid", "argue", "ignore", "meet"]'::jsonb,3,'Standards define the minimum.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.D',4,'A pharmacy that does not follow the board''s rules for safe storage could face:','["disciplinary action", "a holiday", "a raise", "a bonus"]'::jsonb,0,'Violations bring penalties.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.E',3,'Taking continuing education courses and keeping certification current are ways to maintain:','["hours", "competency", "salary", "inventory"]'::jsonb,1,'Learning keeps skills current.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.E',4,'Because new drugs and rules appear often, a technician keeps his skills current through training and:','["time off", "long lunches", "professional organizations", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Organizations offer updates.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.F',3,'Pharmacist, pharmacy technician, and pharmacy buyer are different:','["countries", "seasons", "colors", "career paths in pharmacy"]'::jsonb,3,'Many roles exist.','original'),
('127.472.d.4.F',4,'A technician who wants to become a pharmacist would need to earn a:','["doctor of pharmacy degree", "barber license", "driver''s license", "food permit"]'::jsonb,0,'Pharmacists need a PharmD.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.A',3,'A pill swallowed by mouth is given by the oral route, while a medicine put under the tongue is given by the:','["rectal route", "sublingual route", "nasal route", "topical route"]'::jsonb,1,'Routes describe how drugs enter.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.A',4,'A medicine given by needle into a vein is given by the intravenous route, which sends the drug into the:','["lungs", "skin", "bloodstream", "stomach"]'::jsonb,2,'IV acts quickly.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.B',3,'Antibiotics, analgesics, and antihypertensives are different:','["colors", "sizes", "brands", "classes of drugs"]'::jsonb,3,'Classes group drugs by use.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.B',4,'A drug used to treat infection caused by bacteria belongs to the class called:','["antibiotics", "diuretics", "analgesics", "antihistamines"]'::jsonb,0,'Antibiotics fight bacteria.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.C',3,'In the term gastritis, the root gastr refers to the stomach and the suffix itis means:','["study", "inflammation", "pain", "removal"]'::jsonb,1,'Suffixes carry meaning.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.C',4,'The abbreviation qd on older prescriptions means once a day, and the prefix hypo means:','["above normal", "before", "under or below normal", "after"]'::jsonb,2,'Word parts guide meaning.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.D',3,'The term for how a drug is absorbed, distributed, and removed by the body is:','["inventory", "pharmacy law", "anatomy", "pharmacokinetics"]'::jsonb,3,'Kinetics tracks the drug''s path.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.D',4,'A side effect is an unintended effect of a drug, while the intended benefit is its:','["therapeutic effect", "adverse reaction", "allergy", "overdose"]'::jsonb,0,'Terms differ by intent.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.E',3,'A technician sees a new drug name, antiemetic. Knowing that anti means against and emesis means vomiting, she can figure out that it:','["lowers pain", "prevents vomiting", "causes vomiting", "raises blood sugar"]'::jsonb,1,'Word parts reveal meaning.','original'),
('127.472.d.5.E',4,'Seeing the suffix -itis in a drug use statement lets a technician guess that the drug treats:','["thirst", "infection only", "inflammation", "pain only"]'::jsonb,2,'Roots help understanding.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.A',3,'A pharmacy technician converts 2 tablespoons to teaspoons using 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons. The result is:','["2 teaspoons", "9 teaspoons", "3 teaspoons", "6 teaspoons"]'::jsonb,3,'2 x 3 = 6.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.A',4,'A medicine order calls for 750 mg of a drug supplied in 250 mg tablets. The number of tablets needed is:','["3", "5", "2", "4"]'::jsonb,0,'750 / 250 = 3.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.B',3,'A syringe holds 5 mL. Since 1 L = 1,000 mL, the amount in liters is:','["0.05 L", "0.005 L", "5 L", "0.5 L"]'::jsonb,1,'5 / 1,000 = 0.005.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.B',4,'A dose of 2.5 g converted to milligrams is:','["250 mg", "25,000 mg", "2,500 mg", "25 mg"]'::jsonb,2,'1 g = 1,000 mg.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.C',3,'A patient weighs 110 pounds. Using 1 kg = 2.2 lb, the weight in kilograms is:','["25 kg", "242 kg", "100 kg", "50 kg"]'::jsonb,3,'110 / 2.2 = 50.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.C',4,'Using 1 grain = 65 mg, a 5 grain tablet contains how many milligrams?','["325 mg", "650 mg", "65 mg", "13 mg"]'::jsonb,0,'5 x 65 = 325.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.D',3,'A drug is 20 mg per mL. To give a 60 mg dose, the volume needed is:','["1 mL", "3 mL", "6 mL", "30 mL"]'::jsonb,1,'60 / 20 = 3.','original'),
('127.472.d.6.D',4,'A solution contains 500 mg in 250 mL. The concentration in mg per mL is:','["125 mg/mL", "0.5 mg/mL", "2 mg/mL", "750 mg/mL"]'::jsonb,2,'500 / 250 = 2.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.A',3,'The heart and blood vessels make up the circulatory system, and the lungs are part of the:','["nervous system", "digestive system", "skeletal system", "respiratory system"]'::jsonb,3,'Body systems have distinct parts.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.A',4,'The organ system that removes waste from the blood and makes urine is the:','["urinary system", "nervous system", "endocrine system", "muscular system"]'::jsonb,0,'Kidneys filter blood.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.B',3,'A disease process in which the airways narrow and make breathing hard, such as asthma, affects the:','["skin", "respiratory system", "digestive system", "skeleton"]'::jsonb,1,'Pathophysiology links disease to systems.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.B',4,'High blood pressure that damages arteries over time is a pathology of the:','["urinary system", "skeletal system", "cardiovascular system", "nervous system only"]'::jsonb,2,'Hypertension harms vessels.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.C',3,'Diuretics, which help the body remove extra fluid, affect the:','["bones", "skin only", "eyes", "kidneys and urinary system"]'::jsonb,3,'Drugs target systems.','original'),
('127.472.d.7.C',4,'Bronchodilators, which open the airways, are a drug category that affects the:','["respiratory system", "skeletal system", "urinary system", "digestive system"]'::jsonb,0,'Each category acts on a system.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.A',3,'A pharmacist who gives flu shots follows a schedule of recommended vaccines that depends on a person''s:','["address", "age and health", "hobbies", "favorite color"]'::jsonb,1,'Schedules guide timing.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.A',4,'Counseling a parent about when a child should receive each vaccine is following the recommended:','["dress code", "bus route", "immunization schedule", "grocery list"]'::jsonb,2,'Schedules are published by health authorities.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.B',3,'Some people are exempt from certain vaccines for medical reasons, such as a severe allergy, or for religious or conscientious:','["recipes", "games", "hobbies", "beliefs"]'::jsonb,3,'Exemptions have categories.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.B',4,'A medical exemption from a vaccine usually requires a note from a licensed:','["health provider", "reporter", "neighbor", "coach"]'::jsonb,0,'Providers certify medical reasons.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.C',3,'After a vaccine is given, the provider records the vaccine name, the lot number, the date, and the site of the shot. This is:','["advertising", "documentation", "accounting", "shipping"]'::jsonb,1,'Records are required.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.C',4,'Storing vaccines at the right temperature is a standard step because heat or cold can make them:','["brighter", "louder", "less effective", "tastier"]'::jsonb,2,'Cold chain protects vaccines.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.D',3,'A report system collects data on possible harm after a vaccine so scientists can analyze whether the vaccine caused the:','["sale", "tradition", "holiday", "adverse event"]'::jsonb,3,'Data helps analyze safety.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.D',4,'When reading data on vaccine injuries, a careful student looks at how many people were vaccinated and how rare the:','["reactions are", "brands are", "colors are", "stores are"]'::jsonb,0,'Rates matter in safety data.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.E',3,'Herbal supplements and acupuncture are examples of complementary and alternative medicine. Evaluating them requires looking at:','["popularity alone", "scientific evidence", "advertising slogans", "personal opinions only"]'::jsonb,1,'Evidence determines effectiveness.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.E',4,'A supplement may interact with a prescription drug, so patients should tell their pharmacist about every:','["friend they have", "place they shop", "product they take", "song they like"]'::jsonb,2,'Interactions are a safety risk.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.F',3,'Checking blood pressure and cholesterol at regular intervals helps find problems early. These are examples of:','["advertisements", "fundraisers", "holidays", "health screenings"]'::jsonb,3,'Screenings detect issues.','original'),
('127.472.d.8.F',4,'Public health programs that offer free screenings aim to keep a population healthier by finding disease:','["early", "late", "never", "randomly"]'::jsonb,0,'Early detection improves outcomes.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
